# Keep secrets off Vercel entirely.
#
# GRWM's server-side keys (GEMINI_API_KEY, CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY) belong on the
# Convex deployment, because that is where the code using them runs. Vercel only
# ever needs NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL, which is set as a project env var.
#
# Without this, `vercel deploy` from a local checkout uploads .env and Next
# reports "Detected .env file" during the build — putting secrets somewhere they
# serve no purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local-only artefacts.
.screenshots/
data/context-dev-extractions/
scripts/
